{"name":"Bluey","hex":"#375978","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bluey","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A nickname commonly given to a red-headed person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bluey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bluey (nickname)","blocks":[{"text":"Bluey is Australian slang for a redhead."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluey_(nickname)"},{"title":"Bluey Adams","blocks":[{"text":"Frank Adams, known as Bluey Adams, was an Australian rules football player, who played in the Victorian Football League (VFL) for the Melbourne Football Club."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/40/Frank_%22Bluey%22_Adams.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluey_Adams"},{"title":"Bluey (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Bluey is an Australian animated television series aimed at preschool children, created by Joe Brumm and produced by Ludo Studio in Queensland. It was commissioned by the Australian Broadcasting Corporation and the British Broadcasting Corporation, with BBC Studios holding global distribution and merchandising rights. Bluey premiered on ABC Kids on 1 October 2018. It subsequently made its international debut on Disney Junior in the United States and is available for streaming on Disney+."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/48/Bluey_%282018_TV_series%29_title_card.jpg/330px-Bluey_%282018_TV_series%29_title_card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluey_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Bluey (long-lived dog)","blocks":[{"text":"Bluey was a female Australian Cattle Dog owned by Les and Rosalie Hall of Rochester, Victoria. She holds the Guinness World Record as the oldest verified dog to have ever lived. The record was briefly disputed by Bobi, but Bobi's certification was revoked by Guinness due to the lacking evidence, after veterinarians came forward challenging Bobi's claimed age. Additionally, Bluey's title was also challenged by many other dogs including Max, Chilla, Maggie, and Bella, though they were never verified."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/44/Dog_Bluey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluey_(long-lived_dog)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Beide.jpg/500px-Beide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Beide.jpg/1280px-Beide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Beide.jpg/500px-Beide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bluey and her family are modelled after real-life blue and red Australian cattle dogs or heelers.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeide.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Houses_in_Sherwood%2C_Queensland%2C_2022%2C_10.jpg/500px-Houses_in_Sherwood%2C_Queensland%2C_2022%2C_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Houses_in_Sherwood%2C_Queensland%2C_2022%2C_10.jpg/1280px-Houses_in_Sherwood%2C_Queensland%2C_2022%2C_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Houses_in_Sherwood%2C_Queensland%2C_2022%2C_10.jpg/500px-Houses_in_Sherwood%2C_Queensland%2C_2022%2C_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Queenslander residential architecture inspires the designs of animated houses in the series.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHouses_in_Sherwood%2C_Queensland%2C_2022%2C_10.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Jacaranda_mimosifolia_trees_in_New_Farm_Park%2C_Queensland%2C_08.jpg/500px-Jacaranda_mimosifolia_trees_in_New_Farm_Park%2C_Queensland%2C_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Jacaranda_mimosifolia_trees_in_New_Farm_Park%2C_Queensland%2C_08.jpg/1280px-Jacaranda_mimosifolia_trees_in_New_Farm_Park%2C_Queensland%2C_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Jacaranda_mimosifolia_trees_in_New_Farm_Park%2C_Queensland%2C_08.jpg/500px-Jacaranda_mimosifolia_trees_in_New_Farm_Park%2C_Queensland%2C_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jacaranda trees are featured in the series as an example of flora in Australia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJacaranda_mimosifolia_trees_in_New_Farm_Park%2C_Queensland%2C_08.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Bluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg/500px-Bluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Bluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg/1280px-Bluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Bluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg/500px-Bluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bluey at a children's festival in Dudley, England, in June 2024","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Australian_Cattle_Dog_sitting.jpg/500px-Australian_Cattle_Dog_sitting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Australian_Cattle_Dog_sitting.jpg/1280px-Australian_Cattle_Dog_sitting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Australian_Cattle_Dog_sitting.jpg/500px-Australian_Cattle_Dog_sitting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A blue Australian Cattle Dog (Bluey's breed)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAustralian_Cattle_Dog_sitting.jpg"}],"sounds":{"Bluey":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/EN-AU_ck1_Bluey.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/13/EN-AU_ck1_Bluey.ogg/EN-AU_ck1_Bluey.ogg.mp3"}]}}}